---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PillBadge from '../components/PillBadge.astro';
import DashedCard from '../components/DashedCard.astro';
import CtaBanner from '../components/CtaBanner.astro';
import { ShieldCheck, Lock, EyeOff, ServerOff, Cookie, Cpu, RefreshCw } from 'lucide-astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - HateMyPDF"
  description="Strict zero-upload privacy policy. Process PDFs, convert images, format code, and compute data 100% locally in your browser with zero data retention."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0E0F10] px-6 pt-24 md:pt-28 pb-24 md:px-8 lg:px-12 text-[#E5E5E5]">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center">
        <PillBadge label="PRIVACY FIRST" />
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl">
          Privacy <span class="text-[#22c55e]">Policy</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-400 max-w-xl leading-relaxed">
          Comprehensive breakdown of our client-side architecture, zero-data collection guarantee, and browser security standards.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500">Effective Date: August 1, 2026 • Version 2.4</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Highlights -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <DashedCard class="p-5 bg-[#0E0F10]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-white font-bold text-sm mb-1.5">
            <ServerOff class="w-4 h-4 text-[#22c55e]" />
            <span>Zero Server Uploads</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Your files never leave your computer or transmit across external networks.</p>
        </DashedCard>
        <DashedCard class="p-5 bg-[#0E0F10]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-white font-bold text-sm mb-1.5">
            <Cpu class="w-4 h-4 text-[#22c55e]" />
            <span>100% Local RAM Execution</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">Processing runs on your device CPU/GPU via WebAssembly and Web Workers.</p>
        </DashedCard>
        <DashedCard class="p-5 bg-[#0E0F10]">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-white font-bold text-sm mb-1.5">
            <Cookie class="w-4 h-4 text-[#22c55e]" />
            <span>Cookie-Free Tracking</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">No tracking cookies, no cross-site profiling, and no advertising scripts.</p>
        </DashedCard>
      </div>

      <DashedCard class="mt-8 p-6 sm:p-10 bg-[#0E0F10]">
        <div class="space-y-8 text-sm text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">1.</span> Client-Side WebAssembly Architecture
            </h2>
            <p>
              At <strong>HateMyPDF</strong>, privacy is engineered into our technical foundation rather than added as a policy promise. Every PDF tool, image format converter, developer utility, text processor, and calculator operates 100% locally within your web browser using modern WebAssembly (WASM), HTML5 Canvas, and Web Worker threads.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2">
              When you select or drop a file into any tool, your browser loads that file directly into local device RAM. Processing takes place locally on your hardware. You can verify this anytime by disconnecting your internet connection or inspecting your browser's Developer Tools Network Tab during file execution.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-[#3a3a3b] pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">2.</span> Zero Data Retention & Immediate RAM Purging
            </h2>
            <p>
              Because HateMyPDF does not utilize server upload endpoints for file processing:
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2.5 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-400">
              <li>We never store, inspect, view, or retain copies of your documents, images, or code.</li>
              <li>Your document contents, text inputs, and processed files exist exclusively in transient RAM.</li>
              <li>Once you navigate away, refresh, or close your browser tab, all transient file memory is instantly freed by your operating system's garbage collector.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-[#3a3a3b] pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">3.</span> Cookies, Analytics, & Network Privacy
            </h2>
            <p>
              We maintain a strict cookie-free experience. We do not place tracking cookies, advertising identifiers, or invasive user fingerprinting scripts on your browser.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-neutral-400">
              We monitor anonymous static page request counts (such as aggregate pageview counts) solely to evaluate CDN bandwidth capacity and server infrastructure health. These static request logs contain zero personal information, file details, or user content payloads.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-[#3a3a3b] pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">4.</span> Local Browser Storage & Preferences
            </h2>
            <p>
              Some tools may utilize standard HTML5 <code class="text-[#22c55e] font-mono">localStorage</code> or <code class="text-[#22c55e] font-mono">sessionStorage</code> solely to save non-sensitive local user interface preferences (such as dark mode state or password generator rules). This data resides entirely on your device and can be cleared at any time in your browser settings.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-[#3a3a3b] pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">5.</span> Children's Online Privacy & Compliance
            </h2>
            <p>
              HateMyPDF is suitable for users of all ages. Because we do not collect personal identification information, email addresses, or user files, our platform fully complies with international digital privacy regulations including GDPR, CCPA, and COPPA.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-[#3a3a3b] pt-6">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <span class="text-[#22c55e]">6.</span> Contact & Verification
            </h2>
            <p>
              If you have questions regarding our privacy architecture or wish to audit our client-side processing mechanisms, feel free to inspect our open web assets or reach out to our team at <a href="mailto:privacy@hatemypdf.com" class="text-[#22c55e] hover:underline">privacy@hatemypdf.com</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </DashedCard>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16">
      <CtaBanner />
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
